WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.263
Infinite-width theory, built on tools like the
Neural Tangent Kernel,

00:00:04.343 --> 00:00:08.983
has transformed how we understand deep network
initialisation and training,

00:00:09.063 --> 00:00:12.130
but it has only ever described a network's output.

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:16.536
This paper extends that theory to the network's
input-output Jacobian.

00:00:16.616 --> 00:00:23.900
The authors show that a multilayer perceptron and
its Jacobian jointly converge to a Gaussian process as width grows,

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:27.803
define a Jacobian Neural Tangent Kernel that
governs training,

00:00:27.883 --> 00:00:32.775
and prove that training with a Jacobian
regulariser, so-called robust training,

00:00:32.855 --> 00:00:37.055
behaves in the infinite-width limit like a simple
kernel regression.

00:00:37.135 --> 00:00:41.020
Along the way they explain, for the first time from
this angle,

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:45.300
why Jacobian regularisation makes networks both
accurate and robust.
